---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Projects — Arian Lopez" description="Open source projects by Arian Lopez.">
  <section class="projects-page">
    <h1>Projects</h1>
    <p class="projects-intro">Things I've built.</p>

    <div class="project-card">
      <div class="project-header">
        <span class="project-name">Trabuco</span>
        <span class="project-tag">Open Source</span>
      </div>
      <p class="project-description">
        A CLI &mdash; and a Claude Code plugin &mdash; that generates production-ready Java multi-module Maven projects along with the AI context coding agents need to extend them. One command produces a fully wired Spring Boot codebase plus task-specific prompts, a code-quality specification, and per-agent rule files already configured for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, and GitHub Copilot.
      </p>
      <div class="project-details">
        <h3>Key features</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Production-grade scaffolding</strong> &mdash; Spring Boot 3.4 + Java 21/25 with Spring Data JDBC, Flyway, virtual threads, Testcontainers, Resilience4j, Spotless, ArchUnit boundary tests, OpenAPI, correlation-ID tracing, and Prometheus metrics. PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, or Redis &mdash; all configured with Docker Compose.</li>
          <li><strong>AI Agent module</strong> &mdash; Spring AI scaffolding for tool calling, LLM input/output guardrails, multi-agent orchestration, knowledge-base integration, MCP server, A2A (Agent-to-Agent) protocol, streaming responses, webhook callbacks, scope-based authorization, and rate limiting &mdash; wired and testable from the first commit.</li>
          <li><strong>OIDC Resource Server</strong> &mdash; Spring Security 6 dual filter chain with JWT validation, scope-mapped authorities, and RFC 7807 ProblemDetail handlers. Ships dormant; flip <code>trabuco.auth.enabled=true</code> to validate tokens from Keycloak, Auth0, Okta, Cognito, or generic OIDC.</li>
          <li><strong>Migration of existing repos</strong> &mdash; <code>trabuco migrate</code> transforms a Spring Boot 2.x/3.x repo in place via a 14-phase orchestrated flow with specialist subagents, per-phase approval gates, and atomic rollback via git tags.</li>
          <li><strong>Claude Code plugin</strong> &mdash; Published in Anthropic's community marketplace. Ships 8 skills, 17 specialist subagents (architect, AI-agent expert, migration orchestrator, 14 migration phase specialists), and an MCP server with 25 tools.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="project-tech">
        <span class="tech-tag">Go</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">Anthropic SDK</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">MCP</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">A2A</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">Java</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">Maven</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">Spring Boot</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">Spring AI</span>
      </div>
      <div class="project-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/arianlopezc/Trabuco" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on GitHub &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .projects-page {
    padding: 1rem 0 2rem;
  }

  .projects-intro {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .project-details {
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }

  .project-details h3 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .project-details ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .project-details li {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .project-links {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .project-links a {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
</style>
